         "parameter", " ", "named", " "}]], "InlineFormula"],
     Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Me"}]], "InlineFormula"],
     Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{".", " ", "It", " ", "prints", " ", "with", " ",
         "that", " ", "familiar", " ", "name", ",", " ", "but", " ", "it",
         " ", "is", " ", "an", " ", "inert", " ", "object", " ", "carrying",
         " ", "the", " ", "identity", " ", "of", " ", "its", " ", "model",
         ".", " ", "This", " ", "is", " ", "why", " ", "two", " ", "loaded",
         " ", "models", " ", "can", " ", "both", " ", "contain", " "}]],
      "InlineFormula"], Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Me"}]], "InlineFormula"],
     " without changing one another."}], "Notes"],
  Cell[TextData[
    {"Keep these objects in symbolic amplitude expressions. Apply ",
     ButtonBox["ModelParameterRules", BaseStyle -> "Link",
      ButtonData -> "paclet:HEPCAT/ref/ModelParameterRules"], " to obtain \
numerical values, optionally with different values for selected inputs. \
Assigning a value to an unrelated global symbol called ",
     Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Me"}]], "InlineFormula"],
     " does not change a model-local parameter."}], "Notes"],
  Cell[TextData[{"The three-argument form is the representation stored by the \
model reader: a name, a scope and a domain. Most users should retrieve \
parameters from ", ButtonBox["ReadModel", BaseStyle -> "Link",
      ButtonData -> "paclet:HEPCAT/ref/ReadModel"],
     " rather than manufacture that representation. The ",
     Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"Real\""}]], "InlineFormula"],
     " domain makes the parameter unchanged by complex conjugation."}],
   "Notes"],
  Cell[TextData[{"A name lookup that is missing or ambiguous returns ",
     Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Failure"}]], "InlineFormula"],
     ". It does not create a new declaration. Use ",
     ButtonBox["ModelParameterName", BaseStyle -> "Link",
      ButtonData -> "paclet:HEPCAT/ref/ModelParameterName"], " when you need \
the string name, for example to match parameters while transferring an \
amplitude between models."}], "Notes"], Cell["Examples",
   "PrimaryExamplesSection"],
  Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Load HEPCAT if needed", "ExampleSubsection"],
     Cell["Skip this setup if HEPCAT is already loaded. These examples assume \
the checkout is in ~/code/hepcat; change the paths if yours is elsewhere. \
Evaluate loading in its own cell before the calculation.", "ExampleText"],
     Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Get", "[", "\"~/code/hepcat/source/HEPCAT.wl\"",
         "]", ";", "\n", "modelDirectory", " ", "=", " ",
         "\"~/code/hepcat/models\"", ";"}]], "Input",
      InitializationCell -> True]}, Closed]], Cell["Basic Examples",
   "ExampleSection"], Cell[TextData[{"Retrieve a declared electron mass."}],
   "ExampleText"], Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"qedModel", " ", "=", " ",
